# * check commodities
# ** 1. check commodities succeeds when all commodities are declared
<
commodity $1.
2020-01-01
  (a)  $1
$ hledger -f- check commodities

# ** 2. and otherwise fails
<
2020-01-01
  (a)  $1
$ hledger -f- check commodities
>2 /commodity "\$" has not been declared/
>=1

# ** 3. But commodityless zero amounts will not fail
<
2020-01-01
  (a)  0

$ hledger -f- check commodities
>=0

# ** 4. But zero amounts with undeclared commodities still fail
<
2020-01-01
  (a)  $0

$ hledger -f- check commodities
>2 /commodity "\$" has not been declared/
>=1

# ** 5. The commodities check is enabled in strict mode, ahead of accounts.
$ hledger -f- check -s
>2 /commodity "\$" has not been declared/
>=1

# ** 6. An alias: tag on a commodity directive lets the check accept the aliased symbol.
<
commodity USD1.00
    ; alias: $

2024-01-01
  (a)  $1

$ hledger -f- check commodities


# ** 7. An error on a price directive quotes its amount as written, not restyled.
<
commodity 1 000,00 EUR

2024-01-01
    a    1 000,00 EUR
    b

P 2024-01-02 X 1000,5EUR
$ hledger -f- check commodities
>2 /P 2024-01-02 X 1000,5EUR/
>=1
